input_prompt: Explain what on-device AI means in simple terms.
INFO: Loaded OpenCL library with dlopen.


On-device AI is like having a smart assistant that works on your phone, computer, or other device, instead of sending all your data to the internet. Imagine if you had a robot that could recognize faces or speak in a smart speaker—those are examples of on-device AI. It processes information locally, which means it doesn’t need to connect to the internet or a server. This helps keep your data private, reduces delays, and makes your device work faster. It’s like having a tiny computer that helps you do tasks right where you are, without needing to send everything to the cloud.

